            <div xml:id="d409">

                <pb facs="0498" n="1332" xml:id="pg1332"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 659.119/352</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-08T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 8, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>114. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 798. For Taylor. Your 916, Embassy’s 10964, June 29, 6 p.m. We believe you
                    should make it clear to Seydoux and Cecil that if Denmark assents to our tonnage
                    proposal, good faith will oblige us to make agreement unless fault can be fairly
                    found with some other demand they make, either upon rations or blockade, and
                    this latter does not seem probable as substantially all blockade measures now
                    agreed to and rations only are under discussion. Danes here expect to receive
                    reply respecting tonnage Monday next. Upon what do the English and French base
                    their belief that there is no probability of Danish ships being withdrawn from
                    present trip charters if general agreement fails?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
